{
  "requirement": "`habeas::validate_repository(root)` MUST return a report with the number of discovered requirements, the number of evidence files, and all validation errors for the supplied project. Ordinary invalid evidence MUST be reported in that report; an inaccessible project root MUST return an I/O error.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Implementation**\n- `validate_repository` (src/evidence.rs:119) returns `io::Result<EvidenceReport>` by delegating to `inspect_repository` and returning its `report`. It is re-exported from src/lib.rs.\n- `EvidenceReport` (src/evidence.rs:16) carries `requirements`, `examples`, `evidence_files` and `errors`. These are computed at the end of `inspect_repository_with_progress`:\n  - `requirements` counts the definitions of kind Requirement.\n  - `evidence_files` is the number of discovered `evidence/**/*.json` files, including citation reviews.\n  - `errors` is the accumulated list of validation errors.\n- Ordinary invalid evidence is pushed into `errors` and never turned into an `Err`. Examples are config load failures, book source errors, definition errors, bad JSON, orphan evidence, missing evidence, reference problems and Rust function coverage.\n- An inaccessible root fails at `fs::canonicalize(root)?` on the first line of `inspect_repository_with_progress`. That returns an `io::Error` rather than a report.\n- The additional `examples` count is a small extension. It is covered by `requirements.examples.evidence`, which `inspect_repository_with_progress` also marks `{impl}`, and it does not conflict with this requirement.\n- The `{impl}` markers sit on the struct, on `validate_repository`, and on the inspection functions it delegates to. I found no other code that implements this requirement without a marker.\n\n**Tests**\n- `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` asserts the requirement and evidence-file counts for a valid project, with no errors.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` checks that many kinds of invalid evidence all land in `report.errors` in one `Ok` report. The cases are missing, orphan, malformed JSON, false determination, changed text, bad inputs, and duplicate and empty definitions.\n- `inspection_progress_preserves_validation_and_finishes_each_phase` checks that the report matches `inspect_repository` for both valid and invalid projects.\n- `cited_example_with_a_test_and_matching_evidence_validates` asserts all three counts (1 requirement, 1 example, 2 evidence files).\n- `inaccessible_project_root_is_an_io_error_not_a_report` (tests/evidence_boundaries.rs:568) covers both halves of the failure contract:\n  - A missing root returns `Err` with `ErrorKind::NotFound`.\n  - Invalid evidence under an accessible root returns `Ok` with an error report.\n- `discovered_external_cargo_outputs_validate_freshness_and_obey_disallow` (tests/evidence_boundaries.rs:506) and `fixme_fixture` (tests/commands.rs:119) exercise the public API in integration settings.\n\n**Gaps**\n- Only the `NotFound` I/O failure is tested, not a permission-denied root. This is a minor gap and follows the same code path.\n- I found no FIXME markers and no unmarked implementing code.\n\nThe implementation and the tests satisfy the requirement.",
  "references": "b29e530bf260b1400a1b11fe3542a589c48af5d5952ad5be6bfe6199326d9394",
